we're still researching

137
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,320
and that we're talking
about in this talk.

138
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:45,050
It's a great blog
post to go back to.

139
00:05:45,050 --> 00:05:49,520
But a good way to frame it is
that RLHF seems to be necessary

140
00:05:49,520 --> 00:05:50,580
but is not sufficient.

141
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:53,030
You can't do something
like ChatGPT or Gemini

142
00:05:53,030 --> 00:05:55,070
or Claude with a
technique that--

143
00:05:55,070 --> 00:05:56,785
without something like RLHF.

144
00:05:56,785 --> 00:05:58,910
But it's not the thing--
like, pretraining is still

145
00:05:58,910 --> 00:06:01,820
most of the work, but the
fact that RLHF is needed

146
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:03,535
is really important
to contextualize

147
00:06:03,535 --> 00:06:04,910
all these improvements
that we've

148
00:06:04,910 --> 00:06:08,490
seen in the open in the
