00:06:38,230 --> 00:06:40,980
But the level of
investment that Anthropic

160
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:42,570
has had in these
kind of techniques

161
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:44,760
and showing this kind of
wide-ranging improvements

162
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:48,120
of their models with
RLHF is a kind flag

163
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:50,760
that we can follow to try
to learn how to do alignment

164
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:53,490
with this much precision and
with this much kind of impact

165
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:56,980
as places like Anthropic
or OpenAI will have.

166
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:59,050
One such example is
just a simple quote

167
00:06:59,050 --> 00:07:04,752
from the Llama 2 paper, which
is like the colloquial way

168
00:07:04,752 --> 00:07:06,460
of reading this quote,
which I will read,

169
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:09,350
is that, whoa, RLHF
worked really easily.

170
00:07:09,350 --> 00:07:11,890
And what the quote
is, is "Meanwhile,

171
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:15,070
reinforcement learning,
known for its instability,

172
00:07:15,070 --> 00:07:18,130
seemed a somewhat shadowy field
for those in the NLP research

173
00:07:18,130 --> 00:07:19,050
community.

174
00:07:19,050 --> 00:07:21,610
However, reinforcement learning
proved highly effective,

175
00:07:21,610 --> 00:07:24,520
particularly given its cost
and time effectiveness."

176
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,980
So this is one of the
biggest endorsements of RLHF.

177
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:29,680
And it's always fun for me
because I came from the RL side,

178
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,300
and then I've been learning NLP.

179
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:34,090
But for NLP researchers
to say these things,

180
00:07:34,090 --> 00:07:35,590
like, yes, reinforcement
learning is

181
00:07:35,590 --> 00:07:39,430
known for instability, and
given that it is cost effective

182
00:07:39,430 --> 00:07:42,320
and time effective for an
RL person, that's shocking.

183
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:45,698
It's like, RL has never
been particularly cost

184
00:07:45,698 --> 00:07:46,490
and time effective.

185
00:07:46,490 --> 00:07:49,030
But for in these language
model domain where we're fine

186
00:07:49,030 --> 00:07:51,460
tuning with it rather than
learning from scratch,

187
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:53,620
to have people in NLP
that are saying this

188
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:58,550
is just really striking for
how much impact it can have.

189
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:00,950
And the timeline of
alignment and open alignment

